# The shell profile for the kernel's root image.
#
# sh reads this only with -l, which init passes.
#
# Control flow lives in loadable modules under /dis/sh, not in sh
# itself, so without "load std" a shell can run commands and pipelines
# but has no if, while or for at all -- "for(i in 1 2 3)" fails looking
# for ./for.
load std

# The default path is already (/dis .); stated here so that it is
# written down somewhere a person can read and change.
path=(/dis .)
